    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0114" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1950v02/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.5/6–150: telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States
                        Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Austin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-01T19:00:00-04:00">June 1, 1950—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>287. 1. In view FonMin’s agreement at London that Dels in NY shld discuss
                    question whether there is any realistic and desirable alternative to Trygve Lie
                    as SYG, Dept suggests you initiate talks with UK and Fr Dels this subject on
                    basic position taken in document FM DF–5 (Apr 18).<anchor n="1" xml:id="d42-f1"
                    />
                </p>
                <pb facs="0115" n="99" xml:id="pg99"/>
                <p>2. Dept has noted alternative procedure suggested by Gross in letter to Hickerson
                    May 3<anchor n="2" xml:id="d42-f2"/> in event of deadlock among Big Five. It is
                    suggested that final determination re method of procedure in that event await
                    result of consultations in NY on FonMins’ question.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d42-f3"
                    />
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d42-f1" n="1" xml:id="d42-f1-content">
                <p>See the draft position paper prepared in the Bureau of United Nations Affairs,
                    April 18, <ref target="#pg87">p. 87</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f2" n="2" xml:id="d42-f2-content">
                <p>Not found in Department of State files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f3" n="3" xml:id="d42-f3-content">
                <p>A September meeting of the three ministers in New York was projected for the week
                    preceding the opening of the General Assembly.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
